hadiths[114]{hadithnumber,text}:
"6058","Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrate that he used to see such dreams that would make him ill, until he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""A good dream is from Allah. When any person sees a dream that he likes, he should relate that dream to the one whom he likes. And when any person sees a dream that he dislikes, he should seek refuge with Allah from the evil of that dream and spit three times to his left."
"6059","A good vision is from Allah and a bad dream (hulm) is from the satan; so if one of you sees anything (in a dream) which he dislikes, he should spit on his left side thrice and seek refuge with Allah from its evil, and then it will never harm him. Abu Salama said: I used to see dreams weighing more heavily upon me than a mountain; but since I heard this hadith I don't care for it (its burden). (Using translation from Muslim 2261d)"
"6060","When one of you sees a vision which he dislikes, he must spit on his left (three times), seek refuge in Allah from the devil three times, and turn from the side on which he was lying. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 5022)"
"6061","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""O servants of Allah! Allah has removed sin except for the one who attacks the honor of his brother; such a person will be guilty of sin."" The people asked: ""O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)! If we use medicine, will there be any sin upon us?"" The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""O servants of Allah! Use medicine, for Allah has created a cure for every disease He has created."" They asked: ""O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), what is the best thing that a servant has been given?"" The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""Good character."" Sufyan says: ""Today, there is no better chain of narration on the face of the earth than this."
"6062","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Allah Almighty has sent down a cure along with every disease that He has sent down. Whoever remains unaware of it, remains unaware, and whoever acquires its knowledge, attains its knowledge."
"6063","There is a remedy for every malady, and when the remedy is applied to the disease it is cured with the permission of Allah, the Exalted and Glorious. (Using translation from Muslim 2204)"
"6064","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Use medicine, for Allah Almighty has not sent down any disease except that He has also sent down its cure, except for death and old age."
"6065","The Prophet (peace be upon him) forbade him from doing so. He said: ""We use it as medicine."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""It is not a medicine, it is a disease."
"6066","Fever is due to vehemence of the heat of Hell, so cool it with water. (Using translation from Muslim 2209b)"
"6067","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Fever is a portion of the heat of Hell, so extinguish it with water."
"6068","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'Indeed, fever is a portion of the heat of Hell, so cool it with Zamzam water.'"
"6069","The Prophet (peace be upon him) said (that is, he supplicated): ""O Lord of the people! Remove the affliction from Thabit bin Qais bin Shammas."" Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) took some soil from Bathan, put it in a bowl in which there was water, and sprinkled that water over him."
"6070","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Why do you cause pain to your children by pressing their throats in this way? Use Indian aloeswood (the narrator says: by this is meant “costus”), for in it there are seven types of healing (i.e., it is a cure for seven diseases), one of which is pleurisy (pneumonia). (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) By “costus” is meant “qist.” This has been stated by the Shaykh."
"6071","from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: *""Use the black seed, for in it is healing from every thing except death.""*"
"6072","“The best of your kohl is antimony, for it improves the eyesight and makes the hair (eyelashes) grow.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3497)"
"6073","“The best of your kohl is antimony, for it improves the eyesight and makes the hair (eyelashes) grow.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3497)"
"6074","narrates: Once the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) came to us, and in his blessed hand was a truffle. He (peace be upon him) said: ""This is a part of the manna that was sent down upon the Children of Israel, and its water is a cure for the eyes."
"6075","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty has sent down a cure for every disease He has sent down. It is obligatory upon you to use cow's milk, for the cow eats from every kind of tree (leaf)."
"6076","I will not go away unless you get yourself cupped, for I heard Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: It is a remedy. (Using translation from Muslim 2205a)"
"6077","It was narrated from Anas that the Prophet ﷺ was cupped in the two veins at theside of the neck and the base of the neck. (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3483)"
"6078","AbuHind cupped the Prophet ﷺ in the middle of his head. The Prophet ﷺ said: Banu Bayadah, marry AbuHind (to your daughter), and ask him to marry (his daughter) to you. He said: The best thing by which you treat yourself is cupping. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2102)"
"6079","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) ordered that Ibn Zararah be cauterized."
"6080","""The Prophet ﷺ cauterized As'ad bin Zurarah for Shawkah."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2050)"
"6081","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us from cauterization (branding with fire as a treatment). We got ourselves cau"
"6082","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Some people came and asked the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) about their companion whom they wanted to cauterize. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) remained silent. They asked about this three times, but the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) remained silent. He did not like it."""
"6083","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) had him cauterized with fire, but his blood continued to flow. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) had him cauterized with fire a second time. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The narration transmitted from Sayyiduna Imran bin Husain (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding the prohibition of cauterization is to be understood as pertaining to the early period, and that too in cases where there is no such reason that necessitates it, as the Arabs used to do, and by this is meant wasm (i.e., branding/cauterization). Whereas in the narration transmitted from Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), there is mention of the permissibility of adopting this method due to a reason that later became apparent, and that is that a person’s recovery should not rely solely on it. This is contrary to the view of the one who claims that there is contradiction in the narrations transmitted from the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"6084","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) prayed: “O Allah, include him among them.” Then another person said: “O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), pray to Allah Almighty that He includes me among them.” The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “‘Ukasha has preceded you.”"
"6085","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) saw a ring in a man's hand and asked, ""What is this for?"" He replied, ""It is due to weakness."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""This will only increase your weakness. Take it off, because if you die in this state while wearing it, then you will be entrusted to it."
"6086","I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) saying: ""Whoever hangs an amulet (according to the customs of the Age of Ignorance), may Allah not fulfill his (purpose), and whoever hangs a thread (according to the customs of the Age of Ignorance), may Allah not fulfill it for him."
"6087","“Whoever seeks treatment by cauterization, or with Ruqyah, then he had absolved himself of reliance upon Allah.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3489)"
"6088","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked, ""What is this for?"" He replied, ""Because of weakness."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Do you like that you be entrusted to it? Take it off."
"6089","I saw a large group of people. I thought perhaps this is my ummah. I asked, ""Who are these people?"" It was said, ""These are the people of Musa (peace be upon him)."" Then I saw an even greater multitude of people who filled the horizon of the sky. I asked, ""Who are these people?"" It was said, ""This is your ummah."" I became very happy and pleased at this. Then it was said that after these people, seventy thousand from your ummah will enter Paradise without any reckoning and without any punishment. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) stood up and left. The attendees began to wonder who these people would be, and they discussed this matter among themselves. Then they all agreed that these would be those who were born in Muslim households and always remained Muslim, who never experienced the era of shirk (polytheism). Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) returned, and the people asked him about these people. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: These are those who do not get themselves cauterized (for treatment), do not practice ruqyah (incantations) according to the customs of the age of ignorance, do not seek omens, and place their trust in their Lord. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The reason for the prohibition of cauterization and ruqyah is that the people of the age of ignorance used to practice these, and they believed that, without the command of Allah, people would be cured merely by these two things. So, as long as this reason exists, the prohibition of these two things remains. However, if someone practices them and considers them as a means that, according to Allah's decree, becomes a cause for a person's health, and does not believe that benefit comes solely from these two actions, then doing so will be permissible."
"6090","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) went to a woman who had tied an amulet around her neck. Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pl"
"6091","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade incantations. My uncle used to recite incantations for scorpion stings. He came to the P"
"6092","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said to her: Perform ruqyah, as long as there are no words of shirk (polytheism) in it."
"6093","narrates from his father that in the presence of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), a scorpion stung me, so the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) performed ruqyah (spiritual healing) on me and passed his blessed hand over (the affected area)."
"6094","In the pre-Islamic period we used to apply spells and we asked: Messenger of Allah ! how do you look upon it ? He replied : Submit your spells to me. There is no harm in spells so long as they involve no polytheism. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3886)"
"6095","I not perform for you the ruqyah (spiritual healing) which the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform? I replied: Yes. Sayyida Maymunah (may Allah be pleased with her) recited this: ""In the name of Allah, seeking blessing, I perform ruqyah for you. May Allah grant you healing from every illness that has afflicted you. O Lord of the people, remove the suffering, grant healing, You are the only One who grants healing, there is no healer except You."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The correct thing is that the narrator's name is Azhar bin Sa'd, not Azhar bin Sa'id."
"6096","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) used to perform ruqyah (spiritual healing) and say: ""O Lord of the people! Remove the affliction, healing is in Your Hand, only You can remove this affliction."
"6097","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade ruqyah (spiritual healing). It was submitted, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and"
"6098","(Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The statement of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him): ""Treat her according to the Book of Allah,"" by this he meant that you should treat her in a way that the Book of Allah has declared permissible, because the people before, in the time of ignorance, used to perform ruqyah with such words in which there was shirk (polytheism), so the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) forbade them from performing ruqyah with such words. However, the ruling is different for that which the Book of Allah has declared permissible and in which there is no shirk."
"6099","When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited ruqyah for a sick person, said: “Remove the hardship and suffering. Lord of mankind, and grant healing, for You are the Healer and there is no healing except Your healing; (grant) healing which does not leave any sickness behind.ʿ (Using translation from Aḥmad 565)"
"6100","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: O Ka'b, rather, these are also a part of Allah's decree. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The narrator named Amr bin Harith Hamsi is trustworthy; he is not Amr bin Harith Misri."
"6101","Sayyidah Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) permitted performing ruqyah (spiritual healing) for snake and scorpion bites."
"6102","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) permitted the Banu Amr bin Awf to perform ruqyah (spiritual healing) for snake bites."
"6103","Messenger of Allah (may peace he upon him) commanded me that I should make use of incantation for curing the influence of an evil eye. (Using translation from Muslim 2195c)"
"6104","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ allowed Ruqyah for snakebites and scorpion stings.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3517)"
"6105","I have seen today, even a virgin girl does not have such skin. So Sayyiduna Sahl (may Allah be pleased with him) became ill at that very place, he developed a high fever. He was brought to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). They informed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Sayyiduna Sahl (may Allah be pleased with him) has developed a fever, O Messenger of Allah! He is not even able to come to your service. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to him. Sayyiduna Sahl (may Allah be pleased with him) told him about the incident with ‘Amir bin Rabi’ah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why does one of you want to kill his brother? Do you not know that the evil eye is real? You should perform wudu for him. ‘Amir bin Rabi’ah performed wudu for him, and Sayyiduna Sahl (may Allah be pleased with him) came walking with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as if he had no ailment (i.e., his illness was gone)."
"6106","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Do you accuse anyone?” The people said: “Yes, ‘Amir bin Rabi’ah saw him bathing and said: ‘By Allah! I have not seen even a veiled woman with such good skin.’” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) called ‘Amir bin Rabi’ah and, expressing anger towards him, said: “Why does one of you want to kill his brother? Could you not have prayed for blessing for him? You must perform ghusl (ritual washing) for him.” ‘Amir performed ghusl for him, and Sayyiduna Sahl (may Allah be pleased with him) departed with the riders as if he had no ailment (i.e., his illness was gone). The narrator states: The method of performing ghusl is that a bowl is brought, the person performing ghusl puts both his hands into it, then he washes his face in the bowl (i.e., the water used to wash the face falls back into the bowl), then he puts his right hand into it and washes his chest in the bowl, then he puts his hand in and washes his back, then he takes his left hand and does the same, then he washes both knees in the same way and washes up to the tips of his fingers, then he does the same with his left foot, then before placing the vessel on the ground, he gives it to the person who has been afflicted by the evil eye, then that person rinses his mouth with it, pours the water over his face, pours it over his head, and then turns the bowl upside down behind his back."
"6107","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""The evil eye is real. If anything could change destiny, the evil eye would change it. And when you are asked to perform ghusl (ritual washing), then perform ghusl (i.e., do so to remove the effects of the evil eye).\"""""
"6109","Messenger of Allah (may peace he upon him) commanded me that I should make use of incantation for curing the influence of an evil eye. (Using translation from Muslim 2195c)"
"6110","The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Eat it, for whoever eats by means of false incantations (it is forbidden), but you have eaten by means of a true incantation."""
"6111","Sayyiduna Alaqah bin Sahar al-Sulaiti, and he is from a branch of Sulait bin Tamim."
"6112","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us on an expedition. We passed by a village and asked them for hospitality, but th"
"6115","There is no transitive disease, but he is also reported to have said: A sick person should not be taken to one who is healthy. Abu Salama said that Abu Huraira used to narrate these two (different ahadith) from Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but afterwards Abu Huraira became silent on these words:"" There is no transitive disease,"" but he stuck to this that the sick person should not be taken to one who is healthy. Harith b. Abu Dhubab (and he was the first cousin of Abu Huraira) said: Abu Huraira, I used to hear from you that you narrated to us along with this hadith and the other one also (there is no transitive disease), but now you observe silence about it. You used to say that Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: There is no transitive disease. Abu Huraira denied having any knowledge of that, but he said that the sick camel should not be taken to the healthy one. Harith, however, did not agree with him, which irritated Abu Huraira and he said to him some words in the Abyssinian language. He said to Harith: Do you know what I said to you? He said: No. Abu Huraira said: I simply denied having said it. Abu Salama sad: By my life, Abu Huraira in fact used to report Messenger of Allah ﷺ having said: There is no transitive disease. I do not know whether Abu Huraira has forgotten it or he deemed it an abrogated statement in the light of the other one. (Using translation from Muslim 2221a)"
"6116","There is no infection, no safar, no hama. A desert Arab said: Messenger of Allah, how is it that when the camel is in the sand it is like a deer-then a camel afflicted with scab mixes with it and it is affected by sub? He (the Holy Prophet) said: Who infected the first one? Note: The majority of scholars interpret this to mean that these things in and of themselves do not transmit or cause harm through supernatural or hidden means but that Allah is ultimately in control and any fearful superstition around these is false. (Using translation from Muslim 2220a)"
"6117","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""There is no reality in tiyarah (superstitious omen), haamah (the belief in the owl as a bad omen), contagiousness, or Safar."" A man asked, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)! We take a scab-ridden goat and leave it among the herd, and then the other goats also become scab-ridden."" The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Who afflicted the first one with scabies?"
"6118","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""There is no reality in contagion or bad omens. One camel becomes afflicted with mange, and it infects a hundred other camels with mange, but who afflicted the first one with mange?"
"6119","The narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words) then all the camels become afflicted with mange. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who afflicted the first one with disease? Its life, its calamity, and its sustenance (are in the power of Allah Almighty). (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The word used in the text of the narration ""its calamity"" is not correct; rather, the original word is ""its death,"" however, the narration has been transmitted as ""its calamity."" This point has been mentioned by the Shaykh."
"6120","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took the hand of a leper and put it in the Qas'ah. Then he said: 'Eat in Allah's Name, trusting in Allah and relying upon Him.'"" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1817)"
"6121","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) liked good omens and disliked bad omens."
"6122","“The omen is polytheistic deed and anyone of us may think he sees an omen but Allah will dispel it by means of relying upon Him.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3538)"
"6123","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no reality in superstition; its burden will be upon the one who practices it. If (misfortune) were to exist in anything, it would be in a house, a horse, or a woman."
"6124","I heard Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: There is no divination but the best type is the good omen. It was said to Messenger of Allah ﷺ: What is good omen? Thereupon he said: A good word which one of you hears. (Using translation from Muslim 2223a)"
"6125","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""There is no reality in bad omens, and the best omen is the good word which a person hears.\"""""
"6126","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade people from adopting this practice and used these words: \""Let the birds remain in their nests.\"""""
"6127","The Prophet ﷺ said: There is no hamah, no infection and no evil omen; if there is in anything an evil omen, it is a house, a horse, and a woman. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3921)"
"6128","I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) saying: ""There is no reality in contagion, Safar, and Ghul."
"6129","A person from the Ansar who was amongst the Companions of Messenger of Allah ﷺ reported to me: As we were sitting during the night with Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a meteor shot gave a dazzling light. Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: What did you say in the pre-Islamic days when there was such a shot (of meteor)? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best (the actual position), but we, however, used to say that that very night a great man had been born and a great man had died, whereupon Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: (These meteors) are shot neither at the death of anyone nor on the birth of anyone. Allah, the Exalted and Glorious, issues Command when He decides to do a thing. Then (the Angels) supporting the Throne sing His glory, then sing the dwellers of heaven who are near to them until this glory of God reaches them who are in the heaven of this world. Then those who are near the supporters of the Throne ask these supporters of the Throne: What your Lord has said? And they accordingly inform them what He says. Then the dwellers of heaven seek information from them until this information reaches the heaven of the world. In this process of transmission (the jinn snatches) what he manages to overhear and he carries it to his friends. And when the Angels see the jinn they attack them with meteors. If they narrate only which they manage to snatch that is correct but they alloy it with lies and make additions to it. (Using translation from Muslim 2229a)"
"6130","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'If Allah (SWT) were to withhold rain from His slaves for five years and then send it, some of the people would become disbelievers, saying: ""We have been given rain by the star of Al-Mijdah."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1526)"
"6131","I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Augury from the flight of birds, taking evil omens and the practice of pressomancy pertain to divination. Tarq: It is used in the sense of divination in which women threw stones. 'Iyafah: It means geomancy by drawing lines. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3907)"
"6132","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in the morning prayer at al-Hudaibiyyah after rain which has fallen during the night, and when he finished, he turned to the people and said: Do you know what your Lord has said ? They said: Allah and His Apostle know best. He said: This morning there were among mt servants one who believes in me and one who disbelieves. The one who said: ""We have been given rain by Allah's grace and mercy"" is the one who believes in me and disbelieves in the star ; but the one who said: ""We have been given rain by such and such a rain star,"" is the one who disbelieves in me and believes in the star. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3906)"
"6133","narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is no reality in contagion, the owl, Safar, and the star."
"6134","Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""The keys of Unseen are five which none knows but Allah: None knows what will happen tomorrow but Allah; none knows what is in the wombs (a male child or a female) but Allah; none knows when it will rain but Allah; none knows at what place one will die; none knows when the Hour will be established but Allah."" (See The Qur'an 31:34."") (Using translation from Bukhārī 4697)"
"6135","narrates: Rain fell upon us while we were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) removed his garment for the rain. We said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! Why did you do this? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Because it has just come from the presence of the Lord."
"6136","It is nothing (i. e. it is a mere superstition). They said: Messenger of Allah, they at times narrate to us things which we find true. Thereupon Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: That is a word pertaining to truth which a jinn snatches away and then cackles into the ear of his friend as the hen does. And then they mix in it more than one hundred lies. (Using translation from Muslim 2228b)"
"6137","The narrator's name is Fudayl bin Maysarah."
"6138","I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Allah Almighty had ordained the destiny fifty thousand years before He created the heavens and the earth."
"6139","""Idolaters from the Quraish came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ quarreling about Al-Qadar. So this Ayah was revealed: ""The day they will be dragged on their faces into the Fire (it will be said to them): ""Taste you the touch of Hell."" Verily we have created all things with Qadar. (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2157)"
"6140","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: First, there was only Allah, and there was nothing else besides Him. The Throne was upon the water. Then He wrote everything in the Dhikr (i.e., in the Glorious Qur’an or in the Preserved Tablet). Then He created the heavens and the earth. The narrator says: Meanwhile, a man came and said: O Imran, catch your she-camel, she has broken the rope and gone away. The mirage would have disappeared before that. (Sayyiduna Imran, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates) By Allah! I wish I had left the she-camel (and kept listening to the conversation of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him)."
"6141","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When there are no clouds, can you see the moon on the night of the full moon or the sun?"" The people replied, ""Yes."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah is greater than that."" I asked, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! Where was our Lord before He created the heavens and the earth?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""He was in a place of 'Ama' (meaning it cannot be comprehended); above Him and below Him was emptiness."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) In narrating these words, a person named Hammad bin Salamah made a mistake; he narrated the word 'Ghamam' (cloud), whereas the word is 'Ama', and by this the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) meant that the creation does not have the ability to truly comprehend its Creator, because their Lord existed even when neither time nor place existed, and He cannot be known by time, place, or anything else, because He is the Lord of all these things. Thus, the knowledge of the creation about His essence is as if His essence is veiled in 'Ama' from the knowledge of the creation. This does not mean that Allah was in the state of 'Ama', because this is an attribute that resembles the attributes of the creation."
"6142","The Prophet (peace and"
"6143","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""When Allah Almighty created the creation, He wrote in His Book what He made obligatory upon Himself, and that writing is placed above the Throne (and in it is written): 'Indeed, My mercy prevails over My wrath.'\""(Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): \""It is placed above the Throne,\"" re"
"6144","The narrator is unsure, perhaps the words are:) 'My mercy has outstripped My wrath.' The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said, so this writing is with Allah above the Throne. (The narrator says:) Or perhaps it is as the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said."
"6145","“Verily, Allah when He created the creation, He wrote with His Hand concerning Himself, that: ‘My mercy prevails over My wrath.’” (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3543)"
"6146","“On the day when He created the heavens and the earth, Allah created one hundred (degrees of) mercy, of which He placed one on earth, by virtue of which mothers show compassion to their children and animals as well as the birds show compassion to one another. And He kept back ninety-nine (degrees of) mercy. When the Day of Resurrection comes, Allah will complete this mercy.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4294)"
"6147","“Allah has one hundred (degrees of) mercy, of which He has shared one between all of creation, by virtue of which you show mercy and compassion towards one another and the wild animals show compassion towards their young. And He has kept back ninety-nine (degrees of) mercy by virtue of which He will show mercy to His slaves on the Day of Resurrection.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4293)"
"6148","I heard Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: Allah created mercy in one hundred parts and He retained with Him ninety-nine parts, and He has sent down upon the earth one part, and it is because of this one part that there is mutual love among the creation so much so that the animal lifts up its hoof from its young one, fearing that it might harm it. (Using translation from Muslim 2752a)"
"6149","I found some Companions of Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: Everything is by measure. And he further said: I heard Abdullah b. 'Umar as saying: There is a neasure for everything-even for incapacity and-capability. (Using translation from Muslim 2656)"
"6150","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty has decreed five things for every servant: his sustenance, his death, his deeds, his mark, and his abode (that is, his grave)."
"6151","I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""When Allah Almighty intends to seize the soul of a servant in a certain land, He creates some work for that servant in that area."
"6152","I asked the Prophet ﷺ about the Statement of Allah:-- 'And the sun runs on fixed course for a term (decreed), ' (36.38) He said, ""Its course is underneath ""Allah's Throne."" (Prostration of Sun trees, stars. mentioned in Qur'an and Hadith does not mean like our prostration but it means that these objects are obedient to their Creator (Allah) and they obey for what they have been created for). (Using translation from Bukhārī 4803)"
"6153","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Do you know where the sun goes? The people replied: Allah and His Messenger know best. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: It keeps moving until it reaches its appointed place under the Throne, then it falls into prostration and remains in that state until it is said to it: Raise your head and return to where you came from. So it returns and rises from its place of rising. Then it comes again until it reaches its appointed place under the Throne, then it falls into prostration and remains in the state of prostration until it is said to it: Raise your head and return to where you came from. So it returns and rises from its appointed place. Then it comes and reaches its appointed place under the Throne and falls into prostration, then remains in that state until it is said to it: Raise your head and return to where you came from. It returns and rises from its appointed place, then it keeps moving. People do not see anything wrong in this, until one time it will reach its appointed place under the Throne and it will be said to it: Raise your head and rise from the west. So it will rise from the west. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: Do you know when this will happen? It will be at a time when faith will not benefit anyone who did not believe before, nor anyone who did not earn good through his faith. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The narrator named Ishaq has narrated this hadith in the same way from Yunus bin Ubaid from Ibrahim Taimi, although it is well known that this narration is transmitted from Yunus bin Khabbab from Ibrahim Taimi."
"6154","The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: It goes until it reaches under the Throne, presenting itself before its Lord, then it seeks permission and is granted permission. Soon a time will come when it will seek permission but will not be granted permission. It will plead and request, and when this situation arises, it will be said: Go back, rise from where you set. This is what is meant by Allah Almighty’s statement: “The sun runs on its fixed course. That is the decree of the All-Mighty, the All-Knowing.”"
"6155","The Angels were born out of light and the Jinns were born out of the spark of fire and Adam was born as he has been defined (in the Qur'an) for you (i. e. he is fashioned out of clay). (Using translation from Muslim 2996)"
"6156","I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""There are three types of jinn: one type takes the form of dogs and snakes, one type flies through the air, and one type settles and moves about."
"6157","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) granted him permission and instructed him to take his weapon with him. When he came to his neighborhood, he found his wife standing at the door of the house. He pointed his spear towards the woman. The woman said, ‘Do not be hasty about me; first find out why I have come out.’ The man went inside the house and found a strange and unusual snake there. He killed the snake with his spear and then brought it out, impaled on the spear. The snake was still moving. Sayyiduna Abu Sa’id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I do not know which of the two died first—the man or the snake. The people of his tribe came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said, ‘O Messenger of Allah, pray to Allah to return our companion to us.’ The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ‘Pray for forgiveness for your companion.’ Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ‘Some jinn live in Madinah who have accepted Islam. When you see any of them, warn them three times. If it appears before you after that, then kill it. After warning it three times, then kill it.’"
"6158","The place of a whip in Paradise for any person is better for him than everything that exists between the heavens and the earth."
"6159","The example of this world in comparison to the Hereafter is like that of a person who dips his forefinger into the sea and then examines what it returns with (i.e., how much water it brings back)."
"6160","that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Indeed Allah Most High created Adam from a handful that He took from all of the earth. So the children of Adam come in according with the earth, some of them come red, and white and black, and between that, and the thin, the thick, the filthy, and the clean."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2955)"
"6161","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) took my hand and said, ""Allah Almighty created the soil (that is, the earth) on Saturday, on Sunday He created the mountains in the earth, on Monday He created the trees, on Tuesday He created the disliked things, on Wednesday He created light, on Thursday He spread the animals in the earth, and Sayyiduna Adam (peace be upon him) was created on Friday after Asr; He created the last of creation in the last hour of Friday."
"6162","Sayyiduna Adam (peace be upon him) in His own image; his height wa"
"6163","Sayyiduna Adam (peace be upon him), Ibl"
"6164","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah Almighty created Sayyiduna Adam (peace be upon him), he sneezed. His Lord inspired him to say 'Alhamdulillah' (All praise is due to Allah). So his Lord said to him: May Allah have mercy on you. Because of this, Allah's mercy surpassed His wrath."
"6165","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When Allah Almighty breathed the soul into Sayyiduna Adam (peace be upon him) and it reached his head, he sneezed, so he said: All praise is due to Allah, the Lord of all the worlds. Then Allah Almighty said to him: Allah have mercy on you."
"6166","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: When Allah Almighty has created a servant for Paradise, He makes him do the deeds of the people of Paradise, until that person dies while doing the deeds of the people of Paradise, so Allah Almighty admits him into Paradise. When Allah Almighty has created a servant for Hell, He makes him do the deeds of the people of Hell, until that person dies while doing the deeds of the people of Hell, so Allah Almighty admits him into Hell because of that."
"6167","“When Allah created Adam, He breathed the soul into him, then he sneezed and said: ‘All praise is due to Allah.’ So he praised Allah by His permission. Then His Lord said to him: ‘May Allah have mercy upon you O Adam. Go to those angels – to that gathering of them sitting – so say: 'As-Salamu alaikum.' They said 'Wa Alaikas-Salamu Wa Rahmatullah’. Then he returned to his Lord, He said: ‘This is your greeting and the greeting of your children among each other.’ Then Allah said to him – while His Two Hands were closed – ‘Choose which of them you wish.’ He said: ‘I chose the right My Lord and both of the Hands of my Lord are right, blessed.’ Then He extended it, and there was Adam and his offspring in it.’ So he said: ‘What are these O my Lord?’ He said: ‘These are your offspring?’ Each one of them had his age written between his eyes. But among them there was a man who was the most illuminating of them – or among the most illuminated of them. He said: ‘O Lord! Who is this?’ He said: ‘This is your son Dawud, I wrote forty years for him.’ He said: ‘O Lord! Add to his age.’ He said: ‘That is what I have written for him.’ He said: ‘O Lord! Give him sixty of my years.’ He said: ‘So you shall have it.’” He said: “Then, he resided in Paradise as long as Allah willed, then he was cast from it, so Adam was counting for himself.” He said: “So the Angel of death came to him, and Adam said to him: ‘You are hasty, one-thousand years were written for me.’ He said: ‘Of course! But you gave sixty years to your son Dawud.’ So he rejected, and his offspring rejected, and he forgot, and his offspring forgot.” He said: “So ever since that day, what is written and witnessed has been decreed.” (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3367)"
"6168","Souls are troops collected together and those who familiarised with each other (in the heaven from where these come) would have affinity, with one another (in the world) and those amongst them who opposed each other (in the Heaven) would also be divergent (in the world). (Using translation from Muslim 2638a)"
"6169","that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Indeed Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, created His creation in darkness, then He cast His Light upon them, so whoever is touched by that light he is guided, and whoever is not, he goes astray. It is for this reason that I say that the pens have dried with Allah's knowledge."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2642)"
"6170","The pen has dried. So Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) explained: I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) say this: ""Indeed, Allah created the people in darkness, then He took light from His own light and cast it upon them. So whoever He willed, that light reached him, and whoever He willed, that light did not reach him, even though He knew who the light would not reach and who it would reach. So whoever that light reached, he found guidance, and whoever it did not reach, he went astray."" (Sayyiduna Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, said) For this reason, I say the pen has dried (i.e., the decree of destiny has been decided)."
"6171","The two things that make (Paradise or Hell) obligatory are: whoever says there is no god but Allah (the narrator is unsure, perhaps these are the words), whoever believes in Allah will enter Paradise, and whoever dies associating partners with Allah will enter Hell. Whoever intends to do a good deed and then does it, he will receive a tenfold reward. Whoever intends to do a good deed but does not do it, one good deed will be recorded in his book of deeds. Whoever intends to do an evil deed but does not do it, one good deed will be recorded in his book of deeds. Whoever intends to do an evil deed and then does it, one evil deed will be recorded in his book of deeds, and there will be no increase in it. And whoever spends something extra, its reward will be up to seven hundredfold."
"6172","that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""People are but like a hundred camels, a man can not find a mount (suitable to ride upon) among them."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2872)"
"6173","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Do you not know that Allah Almighty has created a specific creation for Paradise? He made them deserving of Paradise while they were still in the loins of their forefathers. He also created Hell and created its inhabitants while they were still in the loins of their forefathers."
"6174","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, the true and truly inspired one, told us that: 'The creation of one of you is put together in his mother's womb for forty days, then it becomes a clot for a similar length of time, then it becomes a chewed lump of flesh for a similar length of time. Then Allah sends the angel to him and commands him to write down four things. He says: ""Write down his deeds, his life span, his provision, and whether he is doomed (destined for Hell) or blessed (destined for Paradise)."" By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! One of you may do the deeds of the people of Paradise until there is no more than a forearm's length between him and it, then the decree overtakes him and he does the deeds of the people of Hell until there is no more than a forearm's length between him and it, then the decree overtakes him and he does the deeds of the people of Paradise until he enters therein."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 76)"
